    "answer": {
      "short": "$C^2-S^2=1$.\n\nExpand both squares and use $3^x3^{-x}=1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C^2-S^2&=\\frac{(3^x+3^{-x})^2-(3^x-3^{-x})^2}{4}\\\\C^2-S^2&=\\frac{3^{2x}+2+3^{-2x}-(3^{2x}-2+3^{-2x})}{4}\\\\C^2-S^2&=\\frac44\\\\C^2-S^2&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nHere $3^x3^{-x}=3^0=1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
